43740617e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,785,729,400,69,2075,15087,67901,198,78045,69,955,2075,593,284,220,21,87,481,220,17,15,15,20,59,60,1958,678,1931,5109,400,87,2418,220,2619,6724,458,7546,400,77,3,1741,429,400,69,1445,8,284,220,21,77,481,220,17,15,15,20,2418,220,7379,400,77,2418,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe function $f(x)$ satisfies\n\\[f(f(x)) = 6x - 2005\\]for all real numbers $x.$  There exists an integer $n$ such that $f(n) = 6n - 2005.$  Find $n.$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"9b5dd2453e33d710694bea7aa506aba5107605ce80a548140b46970ff00f156c"},"seconds":29.35868191719055,"seed":922388159437968209,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we start by understanding the given functional equation:\n\\[f(f(x)) = 6x - 2005.\\]\n\nWe are also given that there exists an integer \\(n\\) such that:\n\\[f(n) = 6n - 2005.\\]\n\nLet's denote \\(a = f(n)\\). According to the problem, we have:\n\\[a = 6n - 2005.\\]\n\nNow, applying the function \\(f\\) to both sides of \\(a = f(n)\\), we get:\n\\[f(a) = f(f(n)).\\]\n\nUsing the given functional equation \\(f(f(x)) = 6x - 2005\\), we substitute \\(x\\) with \\(n\\):\n\\[f(f(n)) = 6n - 2005.\\]\n\nThus, we have:\n\\[f(a) = 6n - 2005.\\]\n\nSince \\(a = 6n - 2005\\), we substitute \\(a\\) back into the equation:\n\\[f(6n - 2005) = 6n - 2005.\\]\n\nThis implies that \\(6n - 2005\\) is a fixed point of the function \\(f\\). Therefore, we set:\n\\[f(6n - 2005) = 6n - 2005.\\]\n\nTo find \\(n\\), we use the fact that \\(f(n) = 6n - 2005\\) and \\(f(6n - 2005) = 6n - 2005\\). We need to find \\(n\\) such that:\n\\[f(n) = n.\\]\n\nGiven \\(f(n) = 6n - 2005\\), we set:\n\\[6n - 2005 = n.\\]\n\nSolving for \\(n\\), we get:\n\\[6n - n = 2005,\\]\n\\[5n = 2005,\\]\n\\[n = \\frac{2005}{5},\\]\n\\[n = 401.\\]\n\nThus, the integer \\(n\\) is:\n\\[\\boxed{401}.\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{401}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To solve the problem, we start by understanding the given functional equation:\n\\[f(f(x)) = 6x - 2005.\\]\n\nWe are also given that there exists an integer \\(n\\) such that:\n\\[f(n) = 6n - 2005.\\]\n\nLet's denote \\(a = f(n)\\). According to the problem, we have:\n\\[a = 6n - 2005.\\]\n\nNow, applying the function \\(f\\) to both sides of \\(a = f(n)\\), we get:\n\\[f(a) = f(f(n)).\\]\n\nUsing the given functional equation \\(f(f(x)) = 6x - 2005\\), we substitute \\(x\\) with \\(n\\):\n\\[f(f(n)) = 6n - 2005.\\]\n\nThus, we have:\n\\[f(a) = 6n - 2005.\\]\n\nSince \\(a = 6n - 2005\\), we substitute \\(a\\) back into the equation:\n\\[f(6n - 2005) = 6n - 2005.\\]\n\nThis implies that \\(6n - 2005\\) is a fixed point of the function \\(f\\). Therefore, we set:\n\\[f(6n - 2005) = 6n - 2005.\\]\n\nTo find \\(n\\), we use the fact that \\(f(n) = 6n - 2005\\) and \\(f(6n - 2005) = 6n - 2005\\). We need to find \\(n\\) such that:\n\\[f(n) = n.\\]\n\nGiven \\(f(n) = 6n - 2005\\), we set:\n\\[6n - 2005 = n.\\]\n\nSolving for \\(n\\), we get:\n\\[6n - n = 2005,\\]\n\\[5n = 2005,\\]\n\\[n = \\frac{2005}{5},\\]\n\\[n = 401.\\]\n\nThus, the integer \\(n\\) is:\n\\[\\boxed{401}.\\]","id":"intermediate_algebra:569"}
